SCPLAN 1
plan windows-first-host
summary Make the resident Windows app the machine-local orchestration authority while retaining provider CLI execution.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-WINDOWS-FIRST
intent REQ-MCP-CONTROL-PLANE

task app-project-registry
size small
title add machine-local project registry
instruction Persist known project roots and the last active project in machine-local application state; do not move project authority out of .statefulclanker.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-ACTIVE-PROJECT
retrieve desktop/*
retrieve lib/StatefulClanker.Integrations.ps1
accept project registry survives application restart
accept project-local durable state remains under the project root
accept missing project paths remain explicit
end

task app-active-project
size small
title restore and expose the active project
depends app-project-registry
instruction Restore the last active project on startup and make project switching explicit to the UI/control plane.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-ACTIVE-PROJECT
accept existing last active project is restored
accept missing last active project produces a no-active-project state
accept no other project is silently substituted
end

task mcp-resident-http
size medium
title move Streamable HTTP MCP ownership into resident host
depends app-active-project
instruction Make the running Windows host own the loopback MCP endpoint without tying listener lifetime to one project process.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-MCP-CONTROL-PLANE
retrieve mcp/*
accept MCP listener remains running while active project changes
accept requests are visibly scoped to the selected or explicitly requested project
accept endpoint remains loopback/local by default
end

task mcp-stdio-bridge
size medium
title make stdio transport a bridge to the resident host
depends mcp-resident-http
instruction Preserve stdio compatibility while removing independent orchestration authority from the stdio process; bridge requests to the resident app over local IPC.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-MCP-CONTROL-PLANE
accept stdio and HTTP expose the same semantic MCP tools
accept stdio process does not maintain divergent active-project state
end

task ui-project-telemetry
size medium
title build active-project overview telemetry
depends app-active-project
instruction Present active project health and execution telemetry in the Windows UI using the Toaster-style status/metric presentation and provider-GUI-style project navigation.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-WINDOWS-FIRST
accept overview shows worker sessions spawned
accept overview shows critic and validator activity
accept overview shows commits and task state counts
accept overview shows outstanding context and intent escalations
accept telemetry is scoped to the selected project
end
